From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 22:34:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: IMAP/SMTP through a WebSocket-TCP proxy

Browsers cannot open TCP sockets. On wasm32, tokio-wasm-shim's
tokio::net::TcpStream is a tunnel through a WS proxy and
tokio::net::lookup_host resolves via the proxy's /dns/{host} endpoint
(both live in crates/tokio-wasm-shim, not here). TLS still terminates
inside wasm; the proxy only sees ciphertext.

Core keeps the glue: connect_tcp_inner on wasm returns the bare shim
stream (tokio-io-timeout needs real tokio timers, which panic on wasm),
SessionStream is implemented for it, and connect_tcp (proxies) is
native-only. dns.rs needs no change: the shim's lookup_host takes the
same (host, port) pairs.

Also adds chrono wasmbind and pgp wasm feature (JS clock instead of
SystemTime::now which panics on wasm32-unknown-unknown).
